      "title": "Representations and warranties",
      "narration": "A representation is a statement offered as true to the best of the applicant's knowledge. A warranty is a stricter contractual assurance. Maryland law specifically treats statements by or for an insured or annuitant in a life or annuity application as representations, not warranties. That distinction does not excuse false information. Applicants should answer completely and accurately, and producers should follow the correction process when an error is found. Do not teach that every small error automatically voids a policy, or that calling an answer a representation makes it harmless.",
