      "title": "Two Maryland application rules",
      "text": "Insurance §12–207 governs statements in applications for life/health insurance and annuities and includes materiality and specified good-faith underwriting tests. §10–126(a)(2) concerns intentional material misrepresentation or concealment in a producer-license application. The elements are not interchangeable.",
      "example": "A question about an insured’s policy application cannot be answered solely by quoting the producer-license discipline standard.",
